does a business need to have social aims  that's a question that came in from  twitter reader emma  great question and to answer that  if we step back if we look at a bigger  picture if we look at your business from  a 50 000 foot level if we get into the  philosophy of entrepreneurship  then every business  has a social aim because if you're not  helping people with your company then  you're not going to make money  money comes from helping people you help  somebody solve a problem you're going to  have success in your company  so every business needs to have that  kind of social aim if you're in it just  to make money it's never going to happen  for you  now diving deep back into the question  i believe that every entrepreneur has an  obligation a duty the the right to go  out and contribute to their community  beyond what they're doing with their  business  find something that will help nourish  your soul as an entrepreneur and do it  as soon as you can  you don't have to go and invest a lot of  money when you're first starting out you  don't have a lot of money so you don't  have to put it all into some charity  that you believe in you have a duty to  grow your business because the more your  business grows the more of an impact you  can have in your community  but give your time especially at the  beginning do something that makes you  feel good  do something that gives back to your  community forget about the business side  of it it can be great marketing that  people know that you're part of  something that you're helping your  community out they'll want to go with  you  but forget about that  do it because it's the right thing to do  do it because it makes you feel good do  it because it gives you more energy to  go to your work the next day  and know that you're not only helping  your customers but you're helping all  these other people attached to it as  well  find a cause that you believe in that's  tied to your core  i believe in entrepreneurs  so i've helped out organizations like  junior achievement  where they teach young entrepreneurs  high school students how to become  business owners and i was a mentor for a  number of years and now the main cause  i'm involved with with kiva it's micro  loan system where we've helped support  thousands of businesses get started  mostly in africa  to help these businesses get off the  ground help people get out of poverty  through entrepreneurship  help them support their family bring on  a workforce and enrich their communities  that's something i feel good about  and if that helps my business so be it  but i do it because it's the right thing  to do  so i believe  that every business should also have  something where you're contributing back  to your community around a cause that  you believe in again don't do it because  you think it's the right thing to do  don't be strategic in the cause you're  helping out it's got to come from the  heart it's got to be something that  you're passionate about you love this  charity you love what they stand for  and that passion and energy will flow  back into your business and make you a  better entrepreneur and help you build a  better company  i know what that at the start is it's  really hard  you know entrepreneurs are working  80 hours a week 100 hours a week  whatever it is it's crazy it's crazy  hard  if you do just do that you're gonna burn  out  if you don't have anything that  contributes to nourishing your soul and  making you better and and helping you  see the impact that you are able to have  then you're gonna burn out with your  business  you're not gonna make it by dedicating a  little bit of time  just a little bit of time i'm not saying  spend 10 hours a week at a charity  dedicate a little bit of time  to your favorite charity to something  that means something to you something  gets you excited something where you can  see the direct impact of your time and  effort  do that allow your team to do that  you'll build a better company have more  impact have more money and you'll be  more excited about what you're doing  every day believe thanks for the great  great question  for those of you watching you like the  video please give it that thumbs up  below it makes me want to do more videos  for you and if you have a comment about  this video or question for your business  let me know in the comments below and  i'll make a video reply for you thanks  guys i'll see you soon
 

